# Endstop monitor test

Standalone firmware to verify **X, Y, and Z** endstops. Uses per-axis pins and shared settings from [`include/Config.h`](../../include/Config.h):

| Axis | GPIO | Config |
|------|------|--------|
| X | `Config::X::endstopPin` (34) | `Config::endstopDebounceMs`, `Config::endstopPressedIsPinLow` |
| Y | `Config::Y::endstopPin` (35) | same |
| Z | `Config::Z::endstopPin` (13) | same |

Wiring assumption: **normally open** switch to GND with `INPUT_PULLUP` (`endstopPressedIsPinLow = true`) — idle **RELEASED**, pressed **PRESSED**.

Serial prints initial state on boot, then **PRESSED** / **RELEASED** whenever a switch changes.

## Upload and monitor

From the project root:

```bash
pio test -e esp32doit-devkit-v1 -f test_endstop --upload
pio device monitor -b 115200
```

To return to production firmware: `pio run -t upload`.
